      players: 'Exactly two players. Humbug was designed as a high-stakes two-hand whist variant for two people who wanted the rigor of Whist without partners; it is documented in London publications from the 1790s (e.g. The Sporting Magazine).',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck. Ranking: A (High) to 2 (Low).',
      equipment: 'Standard 52-card deck. Ranking: A (High) to 2 (Low).',
      dealing: 'Deal all 52 cards, one at a time. The final card (belonging to the dealer) is turned up to determine the Trump suit. Both players then layout their hand face-up by suit to see the complete game state.',
